<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Romania</h1><p class="st-meta">1881 CE – 1947 CE · capital Bucharest</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Romanian monarchy that doubled its territory after the First World War as Greater Romania, then fell to dictatorship, war and a communist takeover.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/romania">Romania</a> won independence at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> in 1878, and in 1881 Prince Carol of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-hohenzollern-sigmaringen">Hohenzollern-Sigmaringen</a> was crowned king. The kingdom inherited the constitution of 1866 and the territory of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-principalities">United Principalities</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-dobruja">Northern Dobruja</a> added in 1878. It gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-dobruja">Southern Dobruja</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war">Second Balkan War</a> of 1913.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Before 1914 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/romania">Romania</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> run by landowners, exporting grain and oil from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ploiesti">Ploiești</a>, and a great peasant revolt in 1907 was harshly put down. In 1918 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bukovina">Bukovina</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a> joined, creating Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. Land reform and the 1923 constitution followed, but the interwar years saw the fascist Iron Guard and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carol-ii-of-romania">Carol II</a>'s royal dictatorship from 1938.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1940 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/romania">Romania</a> lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bukovina">Bukovina</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ion-antonescu">Ion Antonescu</a> led it into war as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> ally until King Michael's coup of August 1944. Under Soviet pressure the communists took power, and Michael was forced to abdicate on 30 December 1947.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-romania.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Romania" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: AdiJapan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Romania.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1881 CE – 1947 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bucharest</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Carol I, Ferdinand I, Michael I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Romanian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Romanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/moldova">Moldova</a>, <a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regatul României, Romania (1881-1947)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=kingdom-of-romania" aria-label="Kingdom of Romania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5304 607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Romania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5624 863L5602 745M5624 863L5624 863M5624 863